A||||5||Kasdan||Clutchless Shifting.||||1||
Z||000000||Kasdan||09-22-2001||11:54 AM||||I love manuals, but i cant work a clutch for the life of me.  In a recent post, someone said they can shift without using the clutch....explain this to me.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">         <BR>Power Steering, Holley Scoop<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||09-22-2001||12:00 PM||||It's called "floating the gears" and I wouldn't try it too often in an automotive tranny.  It's used by truckers.  Big truck trannies are much heavier duty and can hold up to that.  Besides, truckers know exactly when to shift (they get the rpms right) so they don't grind the gears (very often  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).  If you want a stick but don't know how to shift, you should either practice on something other than your car or stock up on transmissions.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||09-22-2001||12:27 PM||||I've read about clutches that are engaged by a big solenoid or hydraulic piston, triggered by a switch on the shift knob.. basically it'd be just like an automatic, but you get all the benefits of a manual tranny..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||3
Z||000003||rogergarrison||09-22-2001||12:59 PM||||it can be done in an emergency. Fiero shift cables are too sloppy to allow for doing it very much. Just practice using the clutch or youll be trashing your transmission pretty quick.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-22-2001||01:18 PM||||Many large truck and most race manual transmissions don't have syncro's in them. This makes clutchless shifting fairly easy for experienced drivers.<P>The syncro's in most street transmissions make clutchless shifting more dificult and you can do major damage trying it too often. Cable shifted stick is even worse since cable play slightly varies the reaction between shifter and transmission. The play means every shift is slightly diferent depending on diferent factors.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierosound||09-22-2001||01:36 PM||||I think he's referring to the clutchless shifting they now have on Ferraris and race cars.  I'm not sure how that works either... ||||reg||1
